Capital E alone gives the largest negative contribution, especially at a
document start. Lowercase e inside words and E after uppercase letters are
weaker. Nearby syntax and accented prose adjust spaced lowercase e as a
heuristic for symbol versus conjunction use. Short E-initial chunks, acute E,
other-script E spellings, and econ-/elect-/emiss-/equat- stems also respond.
